{% comment %}
  Why choose us (Figma: Standart Product Page → Why Choose Us, 491:17135).

  A tinted band holding three things: a title, a lead row of one white card beside a
  photograph, and a row of small white cards under it. The band runs the full width
  of the viewport while the content stops at the page width, which here is the
  1280px the file draws its two 630px columns and their 20px gutter inside.

  The section owns the band, the photograph and the arrangement. Everything with
  words in it is a block: the title and the lead card are static, standing where the
  layout puts them, and the small cards are the merchant's own list — the file draws
  three, a page that wants four adds one. See `docs/section-settings.md`.

  Built from the kit: ui-feature-card for the small cards, through
  [_ui-feature-card]. The lead card is [_ui-feature-panel], which hosts its own
  heading and copy blocks.

  The file carries several cuts of this band — with the title and without it, with the
  badge on the lead card and without, and on the occasion pages a title with a line of
  copy under it and no lead pair at all, four tighter cards carrying the whole section.
  They are the same section with a block cleared or a switch turned off, not five
  sections, so nothing here is drawn twice.

  The lead row splits into two columns at 990px rather than the theme's usual 750px.
  The card is drawn 630 wide and carries a 40px headline; at 750px it would have 335
  and the headline would be four lines of two words.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="section-background color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} why-choose-us-bg why-choose-us-bg--{{ section.settings.background }}"></div>
<div
  class="section section--{{ section.settings.section_width }} spacing-style color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }}"
  style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}"
  data-testid="why-choose-us-{{ section.id }}"
  {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <div
    class="why-choose-us why-choose-us--on-{{ section.settings.background }} why-choose-us--media-{{ section.settings.media_position }}"
    style="
      --why-choose-us-heading-gap: {{ section.settings.heading_gap }}px;
      --why-choose-us-columns: {{ section.settings.columns }};
      --why-choose-us-columns-md: {{ section.settings.columns_md }};
      --why-choose-us-columns-sm: {{ section.settings.columns_sm }};
      --why-choose-us-card-title: {{ section.settings.card_title_size }}px;
      --why-choose-us-card-gap: {{ section.settings.card_gap }}px;
      --why-choose-us-card-radius: {{ section.settings.card_radius }}px;
      {%- comment -%}
        The card's own fill. [ui-feature-card] reads this variable and falls back
        to white, which is right on a tinted band — the home page stands white
        cards on light blue. A page that runs this row on white needs the other
        way round, and the corporate page draws exactly that, so the fill is the
        merchant's rather than a consequence of which page the section is on.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.card_background != 'white' -%}
        --ui-feature-card-background: var(--ui-color-{{ section.settings.card_background }});
      {%- endif -%}
    "
  >
    <div class="why-choose-us__title">
      {% content_for 'block', type: '_ui-heading', id: 'heading' %}
      {%- comment -%}
        The line under the title. Blank on the cuts that do not draw one, which is
        what the block does with an empty field — no switch needed for a thing whose
        absence is just an empty box.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% content_for 'block', type: '_ui-text', id: 'intro' %}
    </div>

    <div class="why-choose-us__content">
      {%- if section.settings.show_lead -%}
      <div class="why-choose-us__lead">
        {% content_for 'block', type: '_ui-feature-panel', id: 'panel' %}

        <div class="why-choose-us__media">
          {%- if section.settings.image != blank -%}
            {% render 'image', image: section.settings.image, height: 525, class: 'why-choose-us__image' %}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ 'lifestyle-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'why-choose-us__image why-choose-us__image--placeholder' }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="why-choose-us__cards">
        {% content_for 'blocks' %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Why choose us. Mobile first; the lead row splits at 990px, the cards at 750px. */
  .section-background.why-choose-us-bg--purple {
    background-color: var(--ui-color-primary);
  }

  .section-background.why-choose-us-bg--light-blue {
    background-color: var(--ui-color-light-blue);
  }

  .section-background.why-choose-us-bg--white {
    background-color: var(--ui-color-white);
  }

  .why-choose-us {
    /* The 20px between the two columns, and between the cards, is drawn geometry:
       630 + 20 + 630 is the 1280 the page column already caps at. */
    --why-choose-us-tile-gap: 20px;
    --why-choose-us-radius: 20px;

    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--why-choose-us-heading-gap, 48px);
  }

  /*
   * Reached as a child of the section rather than by a class of its own: the
   * heading block owns its type and this owns where it stands, and a descendant
   * selector outweighs the block's own rules without depending on which stylesheet
   * is concatenated last.
   */
  .why-choose-us__title {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--why-choose-us-title-gap, 16px);
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* On the purple band the title is the only thing standing on the colour. */
  .why-choose-us--on-purple {
    --ui-heading-color: var(--ui-color-white);
    --ui-text-color: var(--ui-color-white);
  }

  .why-choose-us__content {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--why-choose-us-tile-gap);
  }

  .why-choose-us__lead {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--why-choose-us-tile-gap);
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 990px) {
    .why-choose-us__lead {
      /* The file draws the two 630 wide inside 1280. As fr they hold that at every
         width, and neither pays the whole of the loss. */
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: stretch;
    }

    .why-choose-us--media-start .why-choose-us__media {
      order: -1;
    }
  }

  .why-choose-us__media {
    display: flex;
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }

  .why-choose-us__image {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 100%;
    /* Stacked, the ratio the file draws sets the height. */
    aspect-ratio: 630 / 525;
    border-radius: var(--why-choose-us-radius);
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .why-choose-us__image--placeholder {
    background-color: var(--ui-color-border-gray);
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 990px) {
    /*
     * Beside the card, the photograph takes whatever height the card ends up,
     * rather than the card and the photograph disagreeing by whatever the copy
     * runs to. The file draws them equal in every cut — 362 where the card ends at
     * the paragraph, 548 where it carries a row of tiles.
     *
     * Taken out of the flow to do it. `block-size: 100%` alone is a percentage of a
     * height the row has not decided yet, so the picture falls back to its own 525
     * and sets the row from underneath: on the cuts whose card is shorter than that
     * the card was being stretched, with 150px of white under the paragraph.
     */
    .why-choose-us__media {
      position: relative;
    }

    .why-choose-us__image {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      inline-size: 100%;
      block-size: 100%;
      aspect-ratio: auto;
    }
  }

  .why-choose-us__cards {
    --ui-feature-card-title-size: var(--why-choose-us-card-title, 24px);
    --ui-feature-card-radius: var(--why-choose-us-card-radius, 20px);

    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--why-choose-us-columns-sm, 1), minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--why-choose-us-card-gap, var(--why-choose-us-tile-gap));
  }

  /*
   * The occasion cut puts these four inside the lead card instead, which leaves
   * this row standing empty — and an empty grid still spends the content gap above
   * it. `:empty` will not do: the block region prints whitespace whether or not it
   * has anything in it, so the test has to be for element children. Weighed one
   * class heavier than the rule above, which it has to undo.
   */
  .why-choose-us .why-choose-us__cards:not(:has(*)) {
    display: none;
  }

  /*
   * Three counts, not two, as `CLAUDE.md` asks. The middle tier keeps the drawn
   * three across — for a row of equals, wrapping to two leaves a lone third card
   * that reads as a mistake — and pays for it by tightening the card instead: at
   * 750px a third of the page column is 210px, which the drawn 24px padding and
   * 24px title do not fit.
   */
  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .why-choose-us__cards {
      --ui-feature-card-padding-inline: 16px;
      --ui-feature-card-gap: 24px;

      /* A ceiling, not a size. A row drawn at 20px stays 20px here; the row drawn
         at 24 comes down to meet it, because that is the tier the cards are
         narrowest in. */
      --ui-feature-card-title-size: min(var(--why-choose-us-card-title, 24px), 20px);

      grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--why-choose-us-columns-md, 3), minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 1200px) {
    .why-choose-us__cards {
      --ui-feature-card-padding-inline: 24px;
      --ui-feature-card-gap: 32px;
      --ui-feature-card-title-size: var(--why-choose-us-card-title, 24px);

      grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--why-choose-us-columns, 3), minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Why choose us",
  "tag": "section",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "_ui-feature-card"
    }
  ],
